sysr> EXPLAIN SELECT s.name, c.title
FROM students s JOIN enrollments e ON s.id = e.student_id JOIN courses c ON e.course_id = c.id;
Optimizer: left-deep DP, interesting orders on, estimator=histogram, M=64 pages | 6 relation sets, 6 splits, 30 plans costed, 6 kept | planning 0.022 ms
-> Project s.name, c.title  (rows=103 cost=30.42ms)
   -> BlockNestedLoopJoin  on e.student_id = s.id (hashed blocks)  (rows=103 cost=30.40ms)
      -> BlockNestedLoopJoin  on c.id = e.course_id (hashed blocks)  (rows=100 cost=20.24ms)
         -> SeqScan courses AS c  (rows=10 cost=10.10ms)
         -> SeqScan enrollments AS e  (rows=100 cost=10.12ms)
      -> SeqScan students AS s  [sorted: s.id]  (rows=100 cost=10.12ms)

sysr> EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT *
FROM students JOIN grades ON students.id = grades.student_id
              JOIN enrollments ON students.id = enrollments.student_id
              JOIN courses ON enrollments.course_id = courses.id
WHERE students.age > 18;
Optimizer: left-deep DP, interesting orders on, estimator=histogram, M=64 pages | 12 relation sets, 18 splits, 112 plans costed, 17 kept | planning 0.060 ms
-> Project students.id, students.name, students.age, grades.student_id, grades.course, grades.grade, enrollments.student_id, enrollments.course_id, enrollments.semester, courses.id, courses.title  (rows=425 cost=41.10ms actual=350)
   -> BlockNestedLoopJoin  on students.id = grades.student_id (hashed blocks)  (rows=425 cost=41.01ms actual=350; inner held in memory)
      -> BlockNestedLoopJoin  on enrollments.course_id = courses.id (hashed blocks)  (rows=82.47 cost=30.40ms actual=70; inner held in memory)
         -> BlockNestedLoopJoin  on enrollments.student_id = students.id (hashed blocks)  (rows=82.47 cost=20.28ms actual=80; inner held in memory)
            -> SeqScan enrollments  (rows=100 cost=10.12ms actual=100)
            -> SeqScan students  filter: students.age > 18  [sorted: students.id]  (rows=80 cost=10.12ms actual=80)
         -> SeqScan courses  (rows=10 cost=10.10ms actual=10)
      -> SeqScan grades  (rows=500 cost=10.50ms actual=500)
Estimated I/O: 7 transfers, 4 seeks  -> 40.70 ms
Measured  I/O: 7 transfers (7 reads, 0 writes), 4 seeks  -> 40.70 ms
Buffer pool: 0 hits, 7 misses, 0 evictions
Execution: 350 rows in 0.30 ms

